17:57:10 run E32 20260918-175710: Can a mid-predator be made to hunt — a badger that takes small prey and vermin without becoming a general large predator? T4 established the constraint: a BENIGN predator never acts on a written relation, because the drive is the caste flag rather than anything settable per unit — badger x groundhog was written forty times for zero combat reports. So one arm flips LARGE_PREDATOR on the badger's castes in memory, which also makes the tool's ecology switch arm it, against a control where the badger stays as shipped. The question is not only whether it hunts but WHAT it attacks: if it becomes a general predator, a mid-predator class needs a size filter on the targets the relation is written to. A season on CTRL, two replicates each, combat logged.
