# E32 -- Can a mid-predator be made to hunt — a badger that takes small prey and vermin without becoming a general large predator? T4 established the constraint: a BENIGN predator never acts on a written relation, because the drive is the caste flag rather than anything settable per unit — badger x groundhog was written forty times for zero combat reports. So one arm flips LARGE_PREDATOR on the badger's castes in memory, which also makes the tool's ecology switch arm it, against a control where the badger stays as shipped. The question is not only whether it hunts but WHAT it attacks: if it becomes a general predator, a mid-predator class needs a size filter on the targets the relation is written to. A season on CTRL, two replicates each, combat logged.
run 20260918-175710 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
commits: DwarfCron 835fddb seasonal-wildlife 41bbd19 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- the flag is the whole switch: the armed arm produces badger kills where the control produces none, and the victims are whatever the relation was written to
- the flag arms it but it hunts indiscriminately: badger kills appear and include animals well above small prey, so a mid-predator needs the target list filtered by size rather than the flag alone
- the flag is not sufficient: no badger kills even when armed — something else gates the hunting drive and T4's reading was incomplete

